Enhance your child's communication with "Storytime with AAC"!nbsp;
This program is designed for children with disabilities who use, or would benefit from, means of communication other than their voice. They use AAC devices, iPads, pictures, pointing, or exchanging pictures to communicate. It is designed for emergent communicators five years old and up (emergent communicators are new/existing AAC users who typically communicate with single words). Open to children of all abilities!nbsp;
A parent/caregiver must accompany the child for all the sessions. Due to limited seating, we request that only 1 caregiver per child attend.
*This program is conducted in collaboration with Something To Say and with support from students in the Speech Language Pathology Program at San José State University.This program is developed to align with the Early Education Quality Standards.ADA Accommodation Requests

